documentation_complete: true

title: 'Sudo - timestamp_timeout value'

description: |-
    Defines the maximum number of minutes that can elapse before <tt>sudo</tt> will ask for a passwd again.
    If set to a value less than 0 the user's time stamp will never expire. Defining 0 means always prompt for a
    password. The default timeout value is 5 minutes, and 15 minutes on Debian and Ubuntu.

interactive: false

type: number

operator: less than or equal

options:
    default: 5
    always_prompt: 0
    1_minute: 1
    2_minutes: 2
    3_minutes: 3
    5_minutes: 5
    15_minutes: 15
